1. **Field_109** (Threat level: 0.13, needs 3 drones) has a very high threat level. Drones already protecting this field (Drone_1, Drone_2, Drone_3, Drone_6, Drone_11, and Drone_14) will be kept there as it is already fully protected.
2. **Field_216** (Threat level: 0.10, needs 6 drones) has many drones currently idle that are close enough to assign. I will assign Drones engaging in idle tasks whose locations can efficiently fulfill this requirement. 
3. Any remaining idle drones will be assigned to the other fields based on their threat levels, starting from the highest available threats that need protection (like Field_41 with a threat level of 0.10).
4. Each drone should ideally remain in the field it is best suited to protect based on their current location status.

